Ladybird renders an SVG image’s content with the force-dark settings
of the page that draws it, so its fills darken like inline SVG fills:
dark fills invert, and light ones stay. Blink does the same. Its
SVGImage::PaintRecordForCurrentFrame() turns on force dark in the
image’s own page (SetForceDarkModeEnabled()), and DarkModeFilter judges
SVG fills (ElementRole::kSVG) with its foreground classifier. Nor does
Blink darken the image as a whole: SVGImage::DrawPatternForContainer()
paints the image as a shader, which ApplyToFlagsIfNeeded() leaves alone.
Gecko and WebKit have no force-dark mode.
